[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196524114","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109726#issuecomment-3196524114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109726","id":3196524114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-hxZS","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T12:30:20Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T12:30:20Z","body":"I'm not against named constants, but things like `Math::sqrt(2.0)` will already be optimized out by compiler (but not in `DEV_ENABLED`, which can be a consideration sometimes).\r\n\r\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/d7f73M4qh","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196524114/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196535177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109726#issuecomment-3196535177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109726","id":3196535177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-h0GJ","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T12:32:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T12:33:35Z","body":"If you have a look at the assembly, I don't think you'll see any difference before / after for non DEV builds.\r\n\r\nGenerally for this kind of optimization, we'd want to see assembly, and profiling / benchmarking.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196535177/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196639353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109726#issuecomment-3196639353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109726","id":3196639353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-iNh5","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T12:48:31Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T12:48:31Z","body":"> If you have a look at the assembly, I don't think you'll see any difference before / after for non DEV builds.\r\n> \r\n> Generally for this kind of optimization, we'd want to see assembly, and profiling / benchmarking.\r\n\r\nSince `Math::sqrt` is not `constexpr`, calls to it cannot be evaluated at compile time. Using `std::sqrt` directly may produce slightly different results. If there were truly no differences, then the existence of predefined constants like `Math::SQRT2` would be unnecessary, as all values would always be computed at runtime.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196639353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197169374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109726#issuecomment-3197169374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109726","id":3197169374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-kO7e","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T14:27:18Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T14:33:45Z","body":"> Since Math::sqrt is not constexpr, calls to it cannot be evaluated at compile time. \r\n\r\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/6365hsYnq\r\n\r\n```\r\nfloat my_sqrt(float f)\r\n{\r\n    return sqrt(f);\r\n}\r\n\r\nfloat func()\r\n{\r\n    return my_sqrt(2.0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe above example is the same but calling through a non constexpr function. It also gets evaluated at compile time.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197169374/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197177700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109726#issuecomment-3197177700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109726","id":3197177700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-kQ9k","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T14:29:37Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T14:29:37Z","body":"It shouldn't matter that it's not `constexpr` as it's inlined, unless there's something weird about the compiler refusing to do that for inlined non-constexpr methods","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197177700/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]